   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Hierarchical clustering analysis of within-scanner SC variability"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from scipy.cluster.hierarchy import dendrogram, linkage\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import ward_tree\n",
    "from sklearn.manifold import TSNE\n",
    "from nireports.reportlets.nuisance import _ward_to_linkage\n",
    "\n",
    "from confounds import get_confounds\n",
    "from simulate_sc import simulate_sc\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fix the random seed the same way as in the defacing registered report (RR)\n",
    "day = 231108  # day and time the journal published our HCPh stage 1 RR\n",
    "time = 105017\n",
    "random_seed = day + time\n",
    "\n",
    "hcph_path = Path(\"/data/datasets/hcph-dataset\")\n",
    "iqms_path = Path(\"/data/derivatives/hcph-mriqc/group_dwi.tsv\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Simulate SC matrices with a set bias"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We will use simulated SC matrices with an artifical set bias in the within-scanner variability to develop a Bland-Altman and hierarchical analyses capable of detecting such biases. Once the methodology is refined, we will apply it on the real HCPh data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Simulated a series of 36 SC matrices of shape: (64x64)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "atlas_dim = 64\n",
    "scale = 0.01\n",
    "shape = 0.5\n",
    "num_sessions = 36\n",
    "\n",
    "SC_matrices = simulate_sc(\n",
    "    atlas_dim=atlas_dim, scale=scale, shape=shape, num_sessions=num_sessions\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Prepare the SC matrices array for input in hierarchical clustering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To prepare the SC matrices array to input it in a hierarchical clustering analysis, we will keep only the lower triangle of each SC matrix and unravel it into a row vector."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "(36, 2016)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Extract the lower triangle of each SC matrix and unravel it into a row vector\n",
    "SC_matrices_tril = np.array(\n",
    "    [SC_matrices[i][np.tril_indices(atlas_dim, k=-1)] for i in range(num_sessions)]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(SC_matrices_tril.shape)\n",
    "# Test whether the shape is as expected\n",
    "assert SC_matrices_tril.shape == (num_sessions, atlas_dim * (atlas_dim - 1) // 2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Perform hierarchical clustering to identify what sessions are more similar"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x700 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Perform hierarchical clustering using Ward's method\n",
    "# linkage_matrix_scipy = linkage(SC_matrices_tril, method=\"ward\") # dendrogram(linkage_matrix) # we pre-registered that we would use scikit-learn\n",
    "\n",
    "children, _, n_leaves, _, distances = ward_tree(SC_matrices_tril, return_distance=True)\n",
    "linkage_matrix = _ward_to_linkage(children, n_leaves, distances)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate and plot the dendrogram\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 7))\n",
    "dendrogram(linkage_matrix)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Dendrogram using Ward's Method\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Session Index\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Distance\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### What factor has an influence on the sessions similarity?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
